From a1e9a93889f20416c18a55cd8187bf62f776e67f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:02:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: fall back to the standard station signal attribute

get_sta_handler() derived cli_RSSI exclusively from
NL80211_STA_INFO_CHAIN_SIGNAL.  Per-chain signal is optional; mac80211_hwsim
and other valid drivers can report only NL80211_STA_INFO_SIGNAL.  In that
case `iw station dump` displays the correct RSSI while the HAL returns zero,
which OneWifi converts to invalid RCPI 255.

Use the standard signed signal value when no per-chain samples were present.
Prefer the existing averaged per-chain result when the driver supplies it.
This makes normal associated-STA metrics, including EasyMesh wireless
backhaul links, reflect the kernel measurement.
---
 wifi_hal_nl80211.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
index da625a19..26a8545d 100644
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -7047,6 +7047,10 @@ static int get_sta_handler(struct nl_msg *msg, void *arg)
 
     if (signals_cnt != 0) {
         rssi = rssi / signals_cnt;
+    } else if (stats[NL80211_STA_INFO_SIGNAL] != NULL) {
+        /* Per-chain signal is optional.  The standard aggregate signal is
+         * signed dBm carried in a u8 netlink attribute. */
+        rssi = (int8_t)nla_get_u8(stats[NL80211_STA_INFO_SIGNAL]);
     }
     associated_dev.cli_RSSI = rssi;
     wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d: RSSI %d\n", __func__, __LINE__, associated_dev.cli_RSSI);
